#EXTM3U
# QA fixture for D-SG-1 (docs/STATUS.md "## Defects", ruling SG1): a list whose
# EVERY row sits in the same two-word group, "United States", so every search
# key ends "... united states". Under the pre-fix ranking any fragment of those
# two words (st, sta, ted, ited, unit, states) matched all 50 rows; under the
# shipping ranking a term found only in the group half must be a whole word.
# The names below are chosen so that the fragment queries have a NON-TRIVIAL
# number of genuine name matches, which is what makes the two counts differ
# in a way a reader can check by eye. Expected counts: tests/test_fixture_sg1.py.
#
# Names that genuinely contain a fragment of "united states":
#   st    -> the five STARZ rows, the two STATE rows, FIRST LOOK TV, HISTORY,
#            TASTEMADE, PLUTO TV WESTERNS                          (11 rows)
#   sta   -> the five STARZ rows, the two STATE rows                ( 7 rows)
#   ted   -> UNITED SPORTS x2, PLUTO TV ANIMATED, LIMITED EDITION TV ( 4 rows)
#   ited  -> UNITED SPORTS x2, LIMITED EDITION TV                    ( 3 rows)
#   unit  -> UNITED SPORTS x2                                        ( 2 rows)
#   starz -> the five STARZ rows; not a fragment of the group name, so the
#            pre-fix and shipping counts agree here                  ( 5 rows)
# Two more that the accepted costs in docs/UX.md 2.6 predict:
#   states      -> a WHOLE word of the group, so it still reaches all 50 rows:
#                  the tier survives, and the count GROWS from `state` (2,
#                  the two STATE names) to `states` (50)
#   united stat -> `united` is a whole group word but `stat` only a fragment
#                  of the other one, and no name carries both: nothing
#                  matches, and the empty state must name "United States"
#                  (Model.groupWordHint) instead of shrugging      ( 0 rows)
# Hosts stay under the reserved .test TLD; nothing here can be fetched.
#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="sg1-01.test" group-title="United States",USA STARZ
